From 5c4b05c89962744ffe23c7b7deee20389ca44129 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:55:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] force-isa: stop stripping VNNI from `avx512`, and fix the
 int8 scale order

Two defects, both invisible until VNNI was actually reachable.

1. VNPU_FORCE_ISA=avx512 cleared VNPU_FEATURE_AVX512VNNI. Forcing the
   baseline ISA must not subtract a feature the host has: the int8 GEMM
   silently fell through to the AVX2 kernel. Measured single-threaded at
   128x768x768 on this box: 20,304 MAC/s forced-avx512 vs 82,395 with VNNI
   enabled, 4.1x, with nothing in the output saying which kernel ran.
   VNPU_FORCE_ISA is documented as the way to make deterministic
   cross-machine comparisons, so every such comparison was measuring AVX2
   and calling it AVX-512. `avx512-novnni` is the arm that wants the
   non-VNNI kernel; it is still available, by name.

2. The VNNI kernel multiplied its scales in the opposite order from
   store_i8_c(): (dot * scale_b) * scale_a against the oracle's
   (dot * scale_a) * scale_b. Commutative, not associative, so it differed
   in the last bit and was the only arm disagreeing with the scalar
   reference. vnpu-isa-parity caught it the moment VNNI became reachable.

Also: forcing an ISA the host cannot execute is now refused by name
instead of executing an illegal instruction. An AVX2-only host (Zen 3,
pre-Skylake) asked for avx512 used to fault inside the first kernel.

tests/bench_kernel.cpp is added because the public bench could not answer
the question that mattered: it calls kernel_gemm_i8_range directly with one
tile and one worker, separating microkernel throughput from tile
construction, pool dispatch and the barrier. It is what showed the 4.1x.

Verified: selftest 16/16 and fuzz 60/0 on unforced, scalar, avx2, avx512
and avx512-novnni; vnpu-isa-parity now reports identical int8 GEMM digests
on all four arms for every shape, including the K%4 and N%16 edges.
---
 CMakeLists.txt          |  11 ++++
 src/core/runtime.cpp    |  59 +++++++++++++++--
 src/kernels/kernels.cpp |  11 +++-
 tests/bench_i8.cpp      |   3 +-
 tests/bench_kernel.cpp  | 136 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 212 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/bench_kernel.cpp

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 13160e8..039c9ee 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -119,6 +119,17 @@ if(VNPU_BUILD_TOOLS)
     target_link_libraries(vnpu-isa-parity PRIVATE ${VNPU_LINK_TARGET} Threads::Threads)
     vnpu_set_warnings(vnpu-isa-parity)
 
+    # Links the STATIC archive on purpose: this one calls the microkernel
+    # directly, and the shared library hides internal symbols.
+    add_executable(vnpu-bench-kernel tests/bench_kernel.cpp)
+    target_include_directories(vnpu-bench-kernel PRIVATE ${VNPU_INCLUDE_DIRS})
+    if(TARGET vnpu_static)
+      target_link_libraries(vnpu-bench-kernel PRIVATE vnpu_static Threads::Threads)
+    else()
+      target_link_libraries(vnpu-bench-kernel PRIVATE ${VNPU_LINK_TARGET} Threads::Threads)
+    endif()
+    vnpu_set_warnings(vnpu-bench-kernel)
+
     add_executable(vnpu-bench-i8 tests/bench_i8.cpp)
     target_include_directories(vnpu-bench-i8 PRIVATE ${VNPU_INCLUDE_DIRS})
     target_link_libraries(vnpu-bench-i8 PRIVATE ${VNPU_LINK_TARGET} Threads::Threads)
diff --git a/src/core/runtime.cpp b/src/core/runtime.cpp
